; LOADPIC/SAVEPIC: a background image loaded onto the canvas, and the
; reverse (saving the canvas -- background image, drawing, turtles --
; out as a PNG). Both need a real window (gdk-pixbuf image decoding/
; encoding happens through a GTK-side callback -- see
; load_canvas_background_image/export_canvas_to_png in ui.c), so this
; example only makes sense run from the actual app, not the headless
; test driver.

LOADPIC "backyard.png   ; any gdk-pixbuf format: PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, ...
                         ; scaled to fill the canvas exactly

REPEAT 4 [FD 400 RT 90]   ; a square drawn on top of the loaded image

eraserect 200 200

SAVEPIC "with_square.png   ; always written as PNG, whatever extension you give
